   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the judiciary law, in relation to stenographers appointed by\nthe Oneida county district attorney",
    "basePrintNo": "S6591",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6591-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §321, Judy L",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6591\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the judiciary law, in relation to stenographers\nappointed by the Oneida county district attorney\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill authorizes the Oneida County District Attorney to appoint five\nstenographers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 321 of the judiciary law to add a new subdi-\nvision k to authorize the Oneida County District Attorney to appoint\nfive stenographers.\n\nSection two provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs a result of discovery reforms enacted in 2019, the Oneida County\nDistrict Attorney has requested this legislation. The enacted discovery\nreforms have increased and accelerated requirements on the District\nAttorney relative to the provision of the minutes from the grand jury to\ndefense counsel, and have created a significant strain on the resources\nof the District Attorney's office.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
